        "combined_title":"ISRMT Seminar: Dispersive decay for the Modified Benjamin-Ono equation with small data: Allison Byars (University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill)",
        "event_subtitle":"Allison Byars (University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill)",
        "event_type":"Livestream \/ Virtual",
        "event_type_id":"24",
        "description":"Abstract:  We study the modified Benjamin-Ono equation for small, localized initial data where no solitons arise.  Unlike the standard Benjamin-Ono equation, the modified version is not known to be completely integrable, so we cannot rely on integrable systems tools. First, to manage the nonlocal Hilbert transform in the linear part of the equation, we split it using positive and negative frequency projections. We then combine wave packet testing of Ifrim and Tataru, the Klainerman\u2013Sobolev vector field method, a normal form transformation, and a bootstrap argument, to establish a global-in-time dispersive decay estimate.\n\n*To request access to the Zoom room, please contact Nathan Hayford at nhayford [ at ] umich.edu.*",
