        "event_type":"Workshop \/ Seminar",
        "event_type_id":"21",
        "description":"Discover the beauty and philosophy of traditional Korean painting (Hangukhwa) through an engaging demonstration. Jiyoung Kim will introduce the history, materials, and artistic principles of Korean painting, explaining how natural materials such as ink, brushes, and traditional paper are used to express harmony with nature.\n\nParticipants will watch two live painting demonstrations\u2014one featuring a traditional Korean painting and another focusing on a simple plum blossom composition that is easy to follow. The plum blossom is a meaningful symbol in Korean art, representing resilience, hope, and the arrival of spring.\n\nJiyoung Kim is an award-winning artist and art instructor who studied painting at Hongik University, where she is currently working on an MFA. Her work has been on display in many galleries in South Korea, Los Angeles, New York and in Michigan.\n\nThis event is part of Korea Week, and is held in partnership with the Ann Arbor District Library and the Korean Cultural Center of Washington D.C. For more information, visit https:\/\/myumi.ch\/9JJ4g.\n\n*If there is anything we can do to make this event accessible to you, please contact us. Please be aware that advance notice is necessary as some accommodations may require more time for the university to arrange.*",
