        "description":"Four-part virtual mini-course | Wednesdays, Sept. 9\u201330 | 6\u20137 p.m. ET\n\nSept. 9 \u2014 What Makes a Healthy Democracy?\nSpeakers: Jenna Bednar and Mara Ostfeld\nFaculty experts Jenna Bednar and Mara Ostfeld explore the core elements of healthy democratic systems, including democratic resilience and the institutions and norms that shape democracies in the U.S. and around the world.\n\nSept. 16 \u2014 The Vote: Elections, Redistricting, and Polarization\nSpeakers: Yanna Krupnikov and Rob Mickey\nHow do elections shape democracy? This session examines the forces influencing elections today, from redistricting and the campaign process to polarization among voters.\n\nSept. 23 \u2014 Democracy Around the Globe\nSpeaker: Dan Slater\nTake a global look at democratic trends, including why some democracies endure while others weaken and the pressures democratic systems face across different regions.\n\nSept. 30 \u2014 Democracy's Information Dilemma: The Effects of Social Media and Misinformation\nSpeakers: Josh Pasek and Cesi Cruz\nExplore how social media and misinformation shape democratic institutions and public perspectives and the challenges they pose for democracies today.",
